A||||5||William||Carpet laying tips||||1||
Z||000000||William||02-16-2001||02:39 AM||||Looks like I will be putting new carpet in this weekend. Has Anyone here Installed ACC or MRMikes carpet? His instructions are not on the his site anymore. I know it said to install right over the old carpet. I don't have any clearance between the seats and the center tunnel area so I'm thinking about cutting out that part of the old carpet. Is the old carpet glued to the new? If anybody has put in carpet or has Mikes old instuctions I would appreciate any tips or advice!!<P>William<BR>85 SE 2m6 (with one sweeeeet intertior!)||||reg||1
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||02-16-2001||03:19 AM||||Personally I'd recommend ripping out everything, and covering the bare sheet metal with a couple of layers of dynamat, and then putting some thermal/sound insulation over that, and then putting new carpet in. I'm sure it could be made to look pretty good, especially if the insulation is cut and formed with tape or something.. <P>this is what I plan on doing, btw...<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000002||gabriel||02-16-2001||07:12 AM||||Jesus, DarkLord!<P>  It that your interior I see on that webpage?  Now that is fine, fine, fine!<P> As far as replacing carpet, I would absolutely remove the old before replacing with new.  It also gives you the chance to see any problems occuring down there, as well.   -g||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||02-16-2001||12:19 PM||||you should take out the old carpet but leave the pad, i dont know if mikes includes the new matting. It should be formed, dont need glued in except behind seats. Console holds the center, kick plate and step cover the other side, just lays up under dash.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||02-16-2001||01:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by gabriel:<BR><B>Jesus, DarkLord!<P>  It that your interior I see on that webpage?  Now that is fine, fine, fine!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Nope, not mine.. there are some cool pics of a Fiero GT with leather Camaro seats, they belong to another forum member.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Alex4mula||02-16-2001||01:40 PM||||I installed my Mr. Mike carpet about two yrs ago. Was the simplest thing. It does not comes with padding. You use your old as padding. You just take seats out, check alignment, spray glue and lay it down. You may want to take the door's bottom trim off. I didn't. It depends on how much extra material you have in the edge. You can trim/cut the carpet to avoid taking them out. The hardest part are the doors because you need to take the panels off and the map pockets if you have them. For the map pockets you may need a special kind of inverted socket tool. I just used pliers but was a pain in the #^@$. Just need to be patient. Other than that no big deal.<BR>You can see my results here: <A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/alexft/Alex4mula/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://community-2.webtv.net/alexft/Alex4mula/index.html</A> <BR>||||reg||1
